1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,702
Hello!

2
00:00:00,702 --> 00:00:05,526
This week you will learn how to manage your time in Reading and Writing,

3
00:00:05,526 --> 00:00:09,948
and how to correct your mistakes in depth after a timed mock test.

4
00:00:11,248 --> 00:00:12,201
Strategy one:

5
00:00:12,201 --> 00:00:13,519
timing in Reading.

6
00:00:13,519 --> 00:00:18,795
Our own suggestion is about seventeen, twenty, and twenty-three minutes.

7
00:00:18,795 --> 00:00:21,506
Passage three is usually the hardest,

8
00:00:21,506 --> 00:00:26,488
so an even split of twenty minutes each can leave you short of time.

9
00:00:27,788 --> 00:00:31,652
Write a provisional answer and come back to it later.

10
00:00:34,952 --> 00:00:36,524
The ninety-second rule:

11
00:00:36,524 --> 00:00:41,582
if you have spent that long on a question and still can't find the answer,

12
00:00:41,582 --> 00:00:44,932
write a provisional answer, mark it, and move on.

13
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:48,896
In the last two minutes, fill in every blank that remains.

14
00:00:50,196 --> 00:00:51,200
Strategy two:

15
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,590
timing in Writing.

16
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:57,763
About twenty minutes for Task 1 and about forty minutes for Task 2,

17
00:00:57,763 --> 00:01:01,932
and in each task leave time for planning and checking.

18
00:01:01,932 --> 00:01:05,484
Don't let Task 1 run into the time for Task 2.

19
00:01:06,784 --> 00:01:10,312
Allocate about forty minutes to Task 2.

20
00:01:13,112 --> 00:01:14,349
Strategy three:

21
00:01:14,349 --> 00:01:17,649
deep error correction with an error log.

22
00:01:17,649 --> 00:01:23,011
Sort your old mistakes into groups, and then proofread in passes.

23
00:01:23,011 --> 00:01:26,559
In pass one, check only verbs and subjects.

24
00:01:26,559 --> 00:01:29,776
In pass two, articles and plural nouns.

25
00:01:29,776 --> 00:01:33,488
In pass three, linking words and punctuation.

26
00:01:34,788 --> 00:01:37,788
The number of visitors has increased.

27
00:01:40,588 --> 00:01:45,148
Many students work part-time, which reduces their study time.

28
00:01:48,448 --> 00:01:52,672
This policy can cause serious damage to the environment.

29
00:01:55,972 --> 00:01:57,057
Strategy four:

30
00:01:57,057 --> 00:02:01,242
after a mock test, mark yourself on the four criteria,

31
00:02:01,242 --> 00:02:06,899
and then choose exactly three goals, starting with your lowest criterion.

32
00:02:06,899 --> 00:02:08,836
Goals must be measurable.

33
00:02:08,836 --> 00:02:12,556
This is only our own estimate, not a real score.

34
00:02:13,856 --> 00:02:18,056
Every body paragraph contains one specific example.

35
00:02:21,356 --> 00:02:22,413
Common mistakes:

36
00:02:22,413 --> 00:02:26,707
splitting Reading evenly into twenty, twenty, and twenty minutes,

37
00:02:26,707 --> 00:02:31,265
getting stuck for four or five minutes on a single gap-fill question,

38
00:02:31,265 --> 00:02:34,436
and setting vague goals such as improve grammar.

39
00:02:35,736 --> 00:02:37,708
Mini quiz, question one.

40
00:02:37,708 --> 00:02:44,940
If you split your time evenly, twenty, twenty, and twenty minutes across three passages,

41
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,748
what is the main risk?

42
00:02:46,748 --> 00:02:48,720
Think for a few seconds.

43
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:53,017
Question two.

44
00:02:53,017 --> 00:02:59,922
You have spent about ninety seconds on a question, and you still haven't found the answer.

45
00:02:59,922 --> 00:03:01,380
What should you do?

46
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,953
Question three.

47
00:03:05,953 --> 00:03:11,976
Which sentence joins two independent clauses with only a comma, A or B?

48
00:03:15,276 --> 00:03:15,959
Answers.

49
00:03:15,959 --> 00:03:16,301
One:

50
00:03:16,301 --> 00:03:22,960
you may run short of time on passage three, because it is usually the hardest.

51
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,302
Two:

52
00:03:23,302 --> 00:03:27,485
write a provisional answer, mark it, and move on.

53
00:03:27,485 --> 00:03:27,998
Three:

54
00:03:27,998 --> 00:03:32,266
A, because it has no linking word after the comma.

55
00:03:32,266 --> 00:03:35,340
Sentence B has so, so it is correct.

56
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:38,195
Summary:

57
00:03:38,195 --> 00:03:42,287
plan your time with clear checkpoints, proofread in passes,

58
00:03:42,287 --> 00:03:44,646
and choose three measurable goals.

59
00:03:44,646 --> 00:03:45,964
One important note:

60
00:03:45,964 --> 00:03:48,946
the mock test is our own shortened version,

61
00:03:48,946 --> 00:03:52,553
so the estimated band may be higher than in reality.

62
00:03:52,553 --> 00:03:55,952
The app does not guarantee your real exam result.
